# Secret. ${SF_SECRETS_DIR}/verifier.env: read ONLY by the `verifier` container (internal identity verifier,
# STACK-2 option C). STRUCTURE ONLY today: the real Sankhya adapter is BLOCKED (BLOCKED_EXTERNAL_SECRET), so the
# service runs in disabled mode (set by the compose file) and answers a uniform denial.
#
# Shared secret between the API and the verifier: random, >= 32 characters, e.g. `openssl rand -hex 32`.
# Staging value only; the API gets the same value in api.env (reserved line, not read yet).
VERIFIER_SHARED_SECRET=REPLACE_LONG_RANDOM_VALUE
#
# The verifier REFUSES TO BOOT when it finds any Sankhya, database, session, SMTP or Sentry setting in its
# environment: do not add them here. When the real adapter is approved and implemented, its minimal Sankhya
# credential subset will be added by a reviewed change (never the worker's full set), together with a restricted
# egress path to the Sankhya hosts. Never commit real values.
